2. STELLAR MASS / IMF: is any IMF heavier than the JAM ceiling allowed by the galaxy's own inner kinematics?
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Salpeter population mass (ATLAS3D XX, r band): law over-predicts the JAM mass inside r12 by median +0.120 dex (mean +0.128); 15/16 galaxies over-predicted
  SLUGGS mass (K-band, ~Kroupa/Chabrier-like): inner excess median +0.084 dex; 10/16 over-predicted
  canonical: outer offset with Salpeter masses +0.0490 (+1.81 sigma); with SLUGGS masses +0.0772 (+2.75 sigma)
  alt      : outer offset with Salpeter masses +0.0346 (+1.28 sigma); with SLUGGS masses +0.0624 (+2.23 sigma)
  stellar mass that nulls each outer offset, relative to the JAM-law ceiling: median +0.303 dex (range -0.34..+0.78); it would over-predict the inner JAM mass by median +0.252 dex
  -> an IMF heavier than the JAM ceiling is excluded by each galaxy's own inner kinematics under the law; an IMF gradient that is bottom-heavy only in the core (the measured sense) lowers the outer stellar mass and enlarges the deficit.

